{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"449c8781c81b80560c48d438c5f04ae254ee1b517926c90172df054d3bb4a434","digest":{"component_or_area":"autodeploy disk pressure reclaim","key_entities":["infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py","rebar-autodeploy.timer","rebar-root-disk-pressure","DISK_PRESSURE_PCT","PRESSURE_PRUNE_MIN_INTERVAL","PRESSURE_PRUNE_TS_FILE","prune_docker_caches","root_disk_pct","reclaim_under_pressure","AUTODEPLOY_DISK_PRESSURE","BUILD_CACHE_KEEP","/etc/rebar/autodeploy.env"],"problem_keywords":["disk pressure","docker prune","autodeploy","root disk","no-op tick","throttle","cache reclaim"],"propositions":["The autodeploy no-op tick (every ~2 min when main is quiescent) does not reclaim docker cache, allowing root disk to climb to 95% and trigger alarm despite earlier deploy-path pruning","prune_docker_caches() must be relocated from line ~245 to line ~150 in autodeploy.sh so it is defined before the line-228 no-op early exit can call it","A pressure-triggered reclaim on the no-op path should fire when root disk usage >= DISK_PRESSURE_PCT (default 80%) and is throttled to at most once per PRESSURE_PRUNE_MIN_INTERVAL (default 600s)","The new reclaim must emit an AUTODEPLOY_DISK_PRESSURE marker via the existing marker() function and must not alter autodeploy's exit code (stays 0) if the prune fails"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787619805310001628,"uuid":"a02f3174-46bd-4dfd-b01a-7bd48d4ac668"}